#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:10
#: f404193d3db64ab3a84d603aac2c54ab
msgid "Video RAM adjustment for high-resolution displays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:13
#: 124e293476cd4bc8a544366980f6e5ba
msgid ""
"When a qube starts, a fixed amount of RAM is allocated to the graphics "
"buffer called video RAM. This buffer needs to be at least as big as the "
"whole desktop, accounting for all displays that are or will be connected to "
"the machine. By default, it is as much as needed for the current display and "
"an additional full HD (FHD) display (1920×1080 8 bit/channel RGBA). This "
"logic fails when the machine has primary display in FHD resolution and, "
"after starting some qubes, a 4K display is connected. If the buffer is too "
"small, and internal desktop resize fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:15
#: bf552241be2343119087b45e85a855a5
msgid "To increase the minimum size of the video RAM buffer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:23
#: 1c031c746de54fe3a4e2f7a0fd06a79b
msgid ""
"Where ``$WIDTH`` × ``$HEIGHT`` is the maximum desktop size that you "
"anticipate needing. For example, if you expect to use a 1080p display and a "
"4k display side-by-side, that is ``(1920 + 3840) × 2160 × 4 / 1024 = "
"48600``, or slightly more than 48 MiB per qube. After making these "
"adjustments, the qubes need to be restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:25
#: 73011cd417214856acd60b0a6cfa6f9d
msgid ""
"In the case of multiple display with different orientations or if you plug/"
"unplug displays, the following code will set correct memory size using "
"xrandr."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:32
#: ad1af5ee892d491190bde925b4d76edd
msgid "The amount of memory allocated per qube is the maximum of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:34
#: d5a76c4a4cfe40f7b383196b4472aa37
msgid "``gui-videoram-min``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:36
#: 30627ceacef54e958084c7959d8ea881
msgid "current display + ``gui-videoram-overhead``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:40
#: 28f8c3ec7878411cbe66f8251ba67432
msgid ""
"Default overhead is about 8 MiB, which is enough for a 1080p display (see "
"above). So, the ``gui-videoram-overhead`` zeroing is not strictly necessary; "
"it only avoids allocating memory that will not be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:44
#: ad68212b5783435a83ceaa823342e3ec
msgid "Xorg configuration to mitigate tearing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:46
#: 53d48e9a7f1a439ea85e0c85b8fe6896
msgid ""
"If video playback is choppy instead of smooth, this could be because the X "
"server is not properly configured. If you have HD graphics, then you could "
"try placing this configuration in ``/etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/90-intel.conf``, "
"and restarting the X server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-configuration.rst:58
